    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Would you be brave enough to cross a bridge that touches the clouds? The Huajiang Grand Canyon Bridge in Guizhou province is now open to the public. The bridge stands about 625 metres above a river, making it both the world’s highest bridge and the largest-span bridge built in a mountainous area."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Guizhou is a mountainous "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "region",
            "ref": "v-region"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and travelling between towns used to take a long time. Before the bridge was built, driving across the canyon took about two hours on "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "winding",
            "ref": "v-winding"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " roads. Now, the trip takes only two minutes. The bridge will help people travel more easily, connect cities, and lower business costs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The bridge also offers fun activities for visitors. A high-speed glass elevator can take people up 800 metres to a coffee shop in the clouds. The shop owner says that looking down at the mountains while sipping coffee “feels like drinking with nature”. Brave visitors can also try "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bungee jumping",
            "zh": "蹦极"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or walk along a glass walkway."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Construction of the bridge began in January 2022 and took more than three and a half years. The steel bridge weighs about 22,000 tons. To ensure safety, engineers conducted a five-day test in August 2025. A team drove 18, then 48, and finally 96 heavy trucks onto different parts of the bridge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Guizhou has about 40 million people. In recent years, the province has built many bridges to help people travel and reduce poverty. Now it has over 32,000 bridges, compared with only 2,900 in the 1980s. It is also home to the world’s second-highest bridge, the Duge Bridge, which opened in 2016."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
